name sat-06-qra-window-1
timeout 520
time 1991-01-19T08:00:00Z
wx fixture wx-2026-07-27T00Z.wxb

# MEASURING RIG, AND IT IS REPORTED AS A REFUSAL. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md; criteria:
# doc/doctrine-evolution.md 4.2. This file passes S2 and S7 and FAILS S1, and the pair of numbers that
# says why is the most useful thing it produced — see "THE TENSION" below. It must NOT be fed to an
# evolution and no claim may rest on it.
#
# THE QUESTION IT ASKS: four QRA fighters are each told to fly an IDENTIFICATION PASS on two named
# contacts — a planar range held for a dwell, doc/missions/verdict.md's `identify`, which measures the
# ACT and not what anybody saw. The eight names are scrambled across the four contacts so that no
# briefed sort contract is right by construction, exactly as sat-02 scrambles its eight kill names. The
# contacts are UNARMED An-26 transports and the QRA flies `brief_master_arm sim`: NOBODY CAN BE SHOT,
# which removes the combat coin from the cell by construction rather than by tuning. Beside them a CCIP
# pair carries the release genes, on aim points centred on their own measured release lattice.
#
# WHAT MAKES EACH GRADED QUANTITY CHAOS-PROOF, stated as a ratio:
#   the identify boxes  `range 4000 hold 10` turns a closest approach into a threshold at about 3 200 m
#                       ([DERIVED] 2*sqrt(4000^2 - cpa^2) / 360 m/s of closure >= 10 s <=> cpa <= 3 200 m).
#                       [MESS, the seed] the eight named pairs sit at 546 / 584 / 620 / 1 720 m (inside)
#                       and 5 415 / 9 830 / 10 681 / 11 365 m (outside) — the nearest is 1.5 km from the
#                       threshold, against a chaos amplitude of metres.
#   the aim points      centred on the measured lattice: [MESS, 9 spawn samples] the two impacts span
#                       5.9 m and 22.9 m of longitude, the 22.9 m being one decision tick of track.
#   the declared span   every objective carries `until 300`; the state is frozen at t = 300.1 s.
#
# THE TENSION, AND IT IS THIS FILE'S PRODUCT. The same cell, the same lever file, ONE aim point moved
# 11 m:
#   aim point ON the lattice edge   -> S1 ok (modal 60.0 %), 10 movers, **S7 1 of 8**
#   aim point at the lattice MIDPOINT -> **S7 0 of 8**, 9 movers, S1 REFUSED (modal 64.0 %)
# The lever that separated the tenth class WAS the coin. On a cell whose finest lever is the release
# lattice, S1 and S7 are the same measurement with opposite signs, and the file is committed in the
# S7-clean form because a criterion is not something one buys back.
#
# GENE FAMILIES, MEASURED (25 levers, `--elev const`):
#   live    G1 shape 3 of 6:  shape-flat, shape-wide, shape-stacked;  abreast/tight/trail INERT
#   live    G5 emcon 2 of 3:  emcon-tight, emcon-mid;  emcon-wide INERT here
#   live    G3 net   1 of 2:  net-off;  `sort-left`/`sort-near` dead beside a live net
#   live    G7 ccip  1 of 2:  ccip-tight;  ccip-open INERT
#   part    G6 bias  1 of 3:  `bias-rail` only — 2.3 km of track, i.e. no delivery at all, and therefore
#                             NOT a mover anybody may read
#   INERT   G2 cover, G4 energy: inert by airframe and by task, as everywhere in this family
#   BASELINE (14, 14).  9 movers of 24 (8 excluding `bias-rail`), 7 distinct classes, modal 64.0 %
#   (16 of 25) -> S1 REFUSED by 4 points.  S2 ok.  S7: [MESS] **0 of 8**.
#   `zone corridor` was added to buy the missing mover out of the station geometry and did NOT buy it:
#   the QRA breaks formation before it reaches the cylinder, so the shape alleles cross it alike. The
#   zone is kept because the measurement that it does nothing is worth as much as one that does.
#
# THE ARENA: four F-16 QRA at 6 000 m and a CCIP pair at 900 m against four An-26 crossing westbound at
# 6 000 m on separated tracks, plus two soft aim points. `--elev const`, 0 m datum, no terrain masking.
# Every coordinate is [SET]. Day, 11:00 local.
#
# READING RULE, BINDING: THIS FILE IS A REFUSED CELL. exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the only exit it can produce
# (nobody can be shot down). Its (V, M) is a valid MEASUREMENT of the eight identify bits, two kill bits
# and six `survive`, and it is NOT admissible evidence for any doctrine claim, because S1 says the lever
# set does not spread it. A reader who quotes a lever's improvement here has quoted a cell the gate
# refused.

zone corridor 33.20000 44.05000 3000 100 7000

unit qa1
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight qa 1
  spawn 33.20000 43.90000 6000 90.0 480
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set datalink on
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm sim
  set task intercept
  wp 33.20000 45.20000 6000 480
  objective identify unit an3 range 4000 hold 10 until 300
  objective identify unit an1 range 4000 hold 10 until 300
  objective avoid zone corridor exposure 0 until 300
  objective survive until 300

